-- title:
--   Lift-valued Hecke system and its χ₋₃-twist are both cuspidal
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $e$ be a group isomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q}) \cong \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$ satisfying the project's predicate [`LanglandsTunnell.DetDictionaryRow`](def/LanglandsTunnell_DetDictionaryRow.html#L11), i.e. for every rational prime $\ell \neq 3$ and every prime $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over $(\ell)$ with finite residue ring and trivial inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$, one has $\det(e(\mathrm{Frob}_Q)) = \ell \bmod 3$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite set $T$ of naturals and of a Hecke eigensystem $\Phi$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ — in this project a level ideal of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$, nonzero, together with two functions $a, b$ on the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$ — with two properties. First, a lift-valuedness table: for every prime $\ell \notin T$ and every prime $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ over $(\ell)$ (prime, lying over, finite quotient, as instances), there is a matrix $M$ in the multiplicative submonoid of $2\times 2$ matrices over $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ generated by the two explicit matrices [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Slift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L21) and [`FLT.ExplicitLift.Tlift`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L23), whose entrywise image under the ring homomorphism [`FLT.ExplicitLift.red`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ExplicitLift.html#L14) ($\sqrt{-2} \mapsto -1$) equals the matrix $e(\mathrm{Frob}_Q)$ over $\mathbb{Z}/3$, and such that $\Phi.a$ at the place of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$ attached to $\ell$ equals $\mathrm{tr}\,M$ and $\Phi.b$ there equals $\det M$. Second, for both $i \in \{0,1\}$ the eigensystem $\Phi$ (for $i = 0$) and its twist by [`LanglandsTunnell.chiNegThreeWeight`](def/LanglandsTunnell_P52Interface.html#L11) (for $i = 1$; the twist multiplies $a$ by $\chi_{-3}$ and $b$ by $\chi_{-3}^2$) satisfies `AutomorphicForm.viaCompactCuspNotion.IsCusp` over $\mathbb{Q}$, which unfolds to: the complex eigensystem obtained through the fixed embedding $\sqrt{-2} \mapsto \sqrt{2}\,i$, read in the raw central normalisation, admits a smooth cusp realisation at the project's compact production pins whose function has the weight-one archimedean character and is archimedean-holomorphic at every real place, and $\Phi.b\,v = \chi_{-3}(\mathrm{N}v)$ for all $v$ outside some finite set.
--
--   This is the octahedral case of the Langlands–Tunnell theorem over $\mathbb{Q}$, here packaged entirely as a statement about Hecke eigensystems with $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$-coefficients rather than about automorphic representations: the mod-$3$ Frobenius data of $e$ are matched with traces and determinants of matrices in the explicit monoid generated by `Slift` and `Tlift`, and weight-one cuspidality is asserted in the project's own sense `viaCompactCuspNotion`, for the eigensystem and for its $\chi_{-3}$-twist simultaneously. Unlike the textbook formulation nothing is claimed about the level of $\Phi$ (in particular no Artin conductor or minimality), nor about uniqueness, nor about which of the two faces corresponds to the representation and which to its contragredient. It feeds the step in which a continuous surjective mod-$3$ Galois representation with cyclotomic determinant, together with a multiplicative set-theoretic lift $\Psi$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$, is realised by a weight-one form of nebentypus $\chi_{-3}$ whose Hecke coefficients are the traces of $\Psi(\rho(\sigma))$.
